SAND TECHNIQUE REFERENCE -- FIFTH KAZEKAGE LINEAGE

Sand manipulation is unique among the Hidden Sand's arts, born of the One-Tail
and perfected by Lord Gaara, the Fifth Kazekage. The practitioner commands fine
sand through chakra, using it as shield, spear, and prison. Gaara's sand is
carried in a gourd of pre-ground desert sand infused with his own chakra.

Catalogued techniques (reference only; not for unauthorized practice):
- Sand Shield / Sand Armour -- automatic defense that guards the user without
  conscious command.
- Sand Binding Coffin -- envelops a target in crushing sand.
- Sand Waterfall / Sand Tsunami -- overwhelming offensive waves of sand.
- Sand Clone -- a body of sand that crumbles and reforms.
- Gold Dust (Third Kazekage / Fourth-era studies) -- a related particulate art,
  denser and rarer than common sand.

Only shinobi bearing an innate or bijuu-derived affinity may attempt sand
control. All others are directed to standard wind-nature training instead.
